From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] tests: use the required format argument in original samples
License: GPL-3.0-only

The v11.0.4 header declares get_int(const char *, ...) and exposes
get_string through a macro that also requires its format argument. Both
original sample programs still use one obsolete zero-argument call.
Supply NULL, which the implementation explicitly treats as no prompt.
Keep both programs, their prompts, input, output and remaining code intact.
This is a generic sample/API compatibility fix, not a RISC-V source fix.
No library implementation change, skipped sample or upstream submission is
claimed. Remove when a fixed official release supplies the format argument.

--- a/tests/get_int.c
+++ b/tests/get_int.c
@@ -4,6 +4,6 @@
 int main(void)
 {
-    int i = get_int();
+    int i = get_int(NULL);
     printf("%i\n", i);
     int j = get_int("Foo: ");
     printf("%i\n", j);
--- a/tests/hackerrank.c
+++ b/tests/hackerrank.c
@@ -4,5 +4,5 @@
 int main(void)
 {
-    string s = get_string();
+    string s = get_string(NULL);
     printf("hello, %s\n", s);
 }
